<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Colorblind Mode theme overlays (FR-01, FR-02).

  Nine styles, one per (type x strength). Each is applied on top of the active
  base theme with `theme.applyStyle(res, force = true)` from ThemeHelper, after
  the Material You block so a wallpaper-derived colorPrimary cannot win back the
  attributes this feature owns.

  EVERY ITEM POINTS AT A @color/ufm_cb_* RESOURCE, AND THAT IS WHY THERE IS NO
  values-night COPY OF THIS FILE. The day/night split is resolved one level down,
  by the colour resources' own values-night variant. Duplicating these styles for
  night would create two copies of the same 43-item mapping and no new
  information. The AMOLED overlay also has no night copy, but for the opposite
  reason: it forces one absolute value in both appearances.

  GENERATED by .plans/tools/gen_colorblind_overlays.py. The base themes in
  themes.xml keep every one of these attributes at its ORIGINAL value, so with
  Colorblind Mode off nothing here is applied and the app's appearance is
  unchanged (FR-19).
-->
<resources>

    <!-- RedGreen / Low. Focus fill clears 3.0:1 against the appearance's worst-case surface.
         Selection and the semantic palette are type-keyed, so they are identical across the three
         strengths of this type and differ only from the other two types. -->
